WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.701
-Our next guest became
the youngest woman

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:05.100
ever to win a gold medal
in the half pipe

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.367
at the 2018 Winter Olympics.

00:00:07.367 --> 00:00:10.100
And soon you can see her
competing for gold again

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.801
at the 2022 Winter Games
in Beijing.

00:00:12.801 --> 00:00:14.767
Ladies and gentlemen,
please welcome the one

00:00:14.767 --> 00:00:19.200
and only Chloe Kim.
Yeah!

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.767
Come on! What!

00:00:21.767 --> 00:00:24.234
-Chloe!
-Hello. Hi.

00:00:24.234 --> 00:00:26.300
-Thank you so much
for doing this

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:27.968
and taking the time
to come see us

00:00:27.968 --> 00:00:30.234
before you're in
the Winter Olympics,

00:00:30.234 --> 00:00:33.501
I mean, opening ceremonies
are a week away.

00:00:33.501 --> 00:00:35.467
Thanks for doing the show.

00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:38.200
How are you feeling right now?
What's going through your head?

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:43.400
-Oh my gosh, it's so crazy.
Like, it's been insane.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:46.501
I actually got all of
my Olympic gear today,

00:00:46.501 --> 00:00:50.100
so I'm really excited did a
little runway show in my house.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.367
-Yeah.
-But it feels so real.

00:00:52.367 --> 00:00:54.300
It's been four years already.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:55.934
-It feels like just yesterday,
kind of.

00:00:55.934 --> 00:00:57.868
I mean, I I have a photo here

00:00:57.868 --> 00:00:59.767
that I wanted to show a view
at six years old

00:00:59.767 --> 00:01:01.234
just so everyone can see.

00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:05.701
It starts young. I mean, look at
you 6 years old, that cute?

00:01:05.701 --> 00:01:07.667
And yeah, and then, yeah,

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:11.033
just to go from there
to this person right here.

00:01:11.033 --> 00:01:12.834
How awesome is that?

00:01:12.834 --> 00:01:17.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.467
After you won, you go like,
"You know what,

00:01:19.467 --> 00:01:21.968
I'm going to take a break
from snowboarding for a second,

00:01:21.968 --> 00:01:23.300
I'm going to go to college."

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:24.734
And everyone was like,
"What?

00:01:24.734 --> 00:01:27.834
No, no, no. You know, you have
to win more medals and do more."

00:01:27.834 --> 00:01:30.734
And you go,
"No, I don't actually.

00:01:30.734 --> 00:01:33.434
I can make my own decisions
and make my own choices,

00:01:33.434 --> 00:01:34.901
and I'm going to go to school."

00:01:34.901 --> 00:01:37.801
And I was like,
"Yeah, respect."

00:01:37.801 --> 00:01:41.033
I love that you did that.
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:43.701
Yeah, school is such
an awesome experience.

00:01:43.701 --> 00:01:46.467
I had so much fun.

00:01:46.467 --> 00:01:51.767
It was just nice to like,
chill and not be sore every day.

00:01:51.767 --> 00:01:53.367
That was the first thing
I noticed. I was like,

00:01:53.367 --> 00:01:57.267
Oh my gosh, I had a very
eventful day and I'm not sore.

00:01:57.267 --> 00:01:59.234
Yeah, like, when does
that ever happen to me?

00:01:59.234 --> 00:02:00.601
So it was really nice.

00:02:00.601 --> 00:02:03.067
Then I met,
I met some amazing people

00:02:03.067 --> 00:02:05.734
and it was just
an amazing experience.

00:02:05.734 --> 00:02:06.968
I'm so happy I did that.

00:02:06.968 --> 00:02:11.033
-What did you major in?
-Oh, okay.

00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:15.167
-Yeah. Talk to me.
-So I went, So oh my gosh. Okay.

00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:20.601
So I went and thinking
I was going to do chemistry.

00:02:20.601 --> 00:02:22.734
-Oh my gosh. Alright.
-Yeah.

00:02:22.734 --> 00:02:25.767
-And that didn't work out?
-No.

00:02:25.767 --> 00:02:28.868
-Yeah.
-Definitely not.

00:02:28.868 --> 00:02:31.234
-Now what is it?
What'd it change to?

00:02:31.234 --> 00:02:35.601
-Yeah. So now I think
I'm going to do anthropology.

00:02:35.601 --> 00:02:38.234
I think.
I-I don't even know.

00:02:38.234 --> 00:02:39.901
Like, I think that's
the whole point, though, like,

00:02:39.901 --> 00:02:43.434
I don't know, but it's awesome.
I love that I don't know.

00:02:43.434 --> 00:02:46.501
Maybe I'll just like, make
a decision super last minute

00:02:46.501 --> 00:02:48.033
when I have to.

00:02:48.033 --> 00:02:51.300
Like, maybe I'll do computer
science. I don't know.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:53.767
Like, I barely like, know how to
turn my computer on, but maybe.

00:02:53.767 --> 00:02:57.133
-That was my major. That was me.
I was computer science.

00:02:57.133 --> 00:02:59.567
That was my major.
-No way. Really?

00:02:59.567 --> 00:03:03.567
-Don't be -- why are you
that surprised?

00:03:03.567 --> 00:03:07.501
-No, it's just I a lot of
my friends that computer science

00:03:07.501 --> 00:03:13.601
and they just looked miserable
every day. So I don't know.

00:03:13.601 --> 00:03:16.200
I applaud you for doing that,
but that's amazing.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:20.067
-They ended up changing my major
and yeah, I of course,

00:03:20.067 --> 00:03:22.534
I end up majoring
in anthropology.

00:03:22.534 --> 00:03:25.868
-Oh, yeah.

00:03:25.868 --> 00:03:29.534
I think you should go
into, like, fashion.

00:03:29.534 --> 00:03:33.901
-That's what I want to do.
-This is like I'm a mind reader.

00:03:33.901 --> 00:03:35.400
-I really want to do that.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:38.000
Yeah, I just don't even know
where to start.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:42.400
I actually made my own
like snow collection with Roxy,

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:46.868
which was such a fun experience
and really inspired me

00:03:46.868 --> 00:03:50.601
to maybe go and do it.
But I do like.

00:03:50.601 --> 00:03:53.400
Why don't you do once you
come up with the fashion line

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:57.067
and sell your stuff
at the store, Anthropologie?

00:03:57.067 --> 00:03:59.067
-Oh my God.
-And there you go.

00:03:59.067 --> 00:04:03.868
Get them all out of the way.
You win, win. It's a win win.

00:04:03.868 --> 00:04:05.934
-Oh my God.
-It's a win win, buddy.

00:04:05.934 --> 00:04:07.067
Call me whatever you want to.

00:04:07.067 --> 00:04:09.634
I'll give you the best advice.
-I will.

00:04:09.634 --> 00:04:10.801
Maybe you can help me

00:04:10.801 --> 00:04:13.300
with the computer stuff
behind the scenes.

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:16.901
Yeah, I'll put you
in touch with someone.

00:04:16.901 --> 00:04:19.467
This is on honor, right?
Cover of "Time" magazine.

00:04:19.467 --> 00:04:21.434
And it's unbelievable
that you can't beat that.

00:04:21.434 --> 00:04:23.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:23.767 --> 00:04:26.234
You don't think, you don't think
you can beat that,

00:04:26.234 --> 00:04:29.267
but then comes along this...

00:04:30.501 --> 00:04:34.701
Cinnamon Toast Crunch, come on!

00:04:34.701 --> 00:04:37.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:37.267 --> 00:04:42.400
That is the biggest honor.
I mean, are you a --

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:45.467
I'm assuming you're a
Cinnamon Toast Crunch fan?

00:04:45.467 --> 00:04:47.234
It was actually concerning.

00:04:47.234 --> 00:04:50.367
Because when I was a kid,
I would eat a box a day

00:04:50.367 --> 00:04:54.467
and my parents would buy them
in bulk pretty much,

00:04:54.467 --> 00:04:55.634
and I would just
go through them.

00:04:55.634 --> 00:04:58.868
So they stopped
buying it for me.

00:04:58.868 --> 00:05:00.300
And here I am now.

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.267
I can have as much as I want
because I'm an adult.

00:05:02.267 --> 00:05:03.901
-That's right. Thank you.
Exactly right.

00:05:03.901 --> 00:05:06.267
[ Applause ]

00:05:06.267 --> 00:05:09.100
Chloe, you know,

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:10.868
we're the biggest fans here
rooting for you.

00:05:10.868 --> 00:05:14.300
And here's what I what I wanted
to just put out open end

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:17.968
whenever you want after you
win the gold. Take time off.

00:05:17.968 --> 00:05:20.167
Do whatever you want.
When you come back to see me,

00:05:20.167 --> 00:05:22.000
let's let's have
a bowl of cereal

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:23.200
and talk about the win.

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:24.834
Okay, bud?
Cinnamon Toast Crunch.

00:05:24.834 --> 00:05:26.133
-That would be so fun.
Let's do it.

00:05:26.133 --> 00:05:28.501
-Alright, bud. We love you.
We're rooting for you.

00:05:28.501 --> 00:05:30.767
I'm so happy you represent
the United States.

00:05:30.767 --> 00:05:33.300
Chloe Kim right there.

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:36.300
The 2022 Winter Olympic Games
begin February 4th.

